Third-party software in the tsdb Pulsar sink (NAR)
==================================================

tsdb itself, including this connector and the tsdb Java client (tsdb-client) packed into the NAR, is licensed under
the Apache License 2.0 (the files LICENSE and NOTICE next to this one).

The NAR also packs the libraries below (META-INF/bundled-dependencies). Their licenses ask that their copyright
notice and license text travel with them; they are reproduced here. The jars keep their own LICENSE and NOTICE
files unchanged, as published.

  zstd-jni 1.5.7-6  (com.github.luben)  BSD-2-Clause. Java bindings of zstd; the jar holds the native library.
  zstd 1.5.7                            BSD-3-Clause (zstd is also offered under GPL-2.0; tsdb uses the BSD License).
                                        The native zstd compiled into zstd-jni.     https://facebook.github.io/zstd/
  jackson-databind, jackson-core,       Apache-2.0. 2.18.2.   https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson
  jackson-annotations                   jackson-core packs a shaded copy of FastDoubleParser (MIT), whose notices are
                                        in META-INF of the jackson-core jar.

The Pulsar runtime provides the Pulsar client and API libraries (Apache-2.0); they are not packed.

docs/licenses.md in the source repository lists every dependency of tsdb.


